{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U3"],
      "pins": ["U3.2", "U3.3"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "VCC"],
      "observed": "The LM1117-5.0 regulator U3 has both its input (pin 3, VIN) and its output (pin 2, VOUT) connected to the same +5V power flag; the +5V rail is also the board's main input (J1 PWR pin 2). The separate VCC rail used by the fan high-side switch and the analog pull-ups (R2, C3, C1, JP2.2, Q3.2) is not connected to the regulator output at all.",
      "expected": "By the part's own metadata a 5.0 V LDO needs VIN higher than VOUT (input+dropout) and its VOUT must drive the regulated VCC rail. Tying VIN to the same +5V net as VOUT bypasses/shorts the regulator and leaves VCC without a source.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "U3 ... pin3 VIN '+5V' ... pin2 VOUT '+5V' ... 'LM1117-5.0' (sheet /, page 2 top)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J1 PWR pin2 '+5V' (sheet /, page 1)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "VCC net on R2, C3 100nF, C1 100nF, JP2.2, Q3.2 (sheet /, page 1 top-right / mid)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator performs no regulation and its input is shorted to its output; the VCC rail that powers the fan P-FET source and the analog pull-up network is left undriven, so the fan high-side switch has no supply and the board's regulated rail is missing.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["J2", "J6", "J3", "U4", "U2"],
      "pins": ["J2.1", "J2.2", "J6.2", "J3.4", "U4.5", "U2.5"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0008"],
      "observed": "The I2C_PWR jumper J2 bridges +5V (pin 1) to NET0008 (pin 2). NET0008 is the MOSI/ISP line, also wired to J3.4 (MOSI), J6.2 and MCU pin 5 (PB0/MOSI).",
      "expected": "A power-enable jumper should not connect the +5V supply to a SPI data / ISP programming line; MOSI must remain a data net driven by the MCU.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J2 'I2C_PWR' pin1 '+5V', pin2 'NET0008' (sheet /, page 1 top)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J3 AVR-ISP-6 pin4 'MOSI' 'NET0008'; U4 pin5 'NET0008' (sheet /, page 1/2)"}
      ],
      "impact": "When J2 is closed, +5V is shorted onto the MOSI/ISP net, conflicting with the MCU's PB0 output and corrupting/shorting the in-circuit programming line.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing supports an anomaly: the LM1117-5.0 regulator U3 has its VIN and VOUT both tied to the +5V rail (so it is bypassed/shorted and the VCC rail it should supply is undriven), and the I2C_PWR jumper J2 shorts +5V onto the MOSI/ISP net."
}

